WEBVTT

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.190
Thank you.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.820
Sir, Crude and Marley's, I believe.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:46.480
Yes, sir.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.200
Is there anything I can do for you, sir?

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:52.980
Well, if it is quite convenient, I should like to speak with a member of the firm.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:53.420
Hmm?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.130
You, uh, you wish to see me, I presume, sir?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.790
Yes. Have I the pleasure of addressing Mr. Scrooge or Mr. Marley?

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.110
Mr. Marley's been dead these seven years.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:06.730
Oh.

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:12.070
Dead as a doornail. Died seven years ago. It's very nice.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.600
We took the liberty of calling on you at your chambers, Mr. Scrooge,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.940
thinking that you would have finished business for the day,

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.610
but we failed to make anyone here.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.230
That's not surprising. I'm the only person who lives there.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.040
Quite. Consequently, we have called here.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.970
At this festive season of the year, Mr. Scrooge,

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:37.980
It seems more than usually desirable to make some slight provision for the poor and destitute who suffer terribly at this present time.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.890
Many thousands are in want of common necessities. Hundreds of thousands are in want of common comforts, sir.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.260
Are there no prisons?

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.320
Yes, plenty of prisons.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.730
The union workhouses are still in operation, eh?

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.110
They are still. I wish I could say they were not.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.970
Warlord and the treadmill are in full victory.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.800
Both very busy, sir.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:02.720
Very glad to hear it, sir.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.620
I thought from what you said that something had occurred to interfere with them in their useful course.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.340
Very glad to hear it, sir. Very glad to hear it.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:13.070
Under the impression that they scarcely furnish Christmas cheer of mind and body for the multitude,

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:19.640
some few of us are endeavouring to raise a fund to buy the poor of London pudding and drink and means of warmth.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:25.140
We choose this time because this is the time of all others when want is keenly felt and abundance rejoices.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.480
Now, what shall I put you down for?

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:30.640
Nothing.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.340
Nothing?

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:34.840
Oh, I see.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.440
You wish to be anonymous.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.110
I wish to be left alone, sir.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.140
Since you ask me what is my wish, that is my answer.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.160
I don't make many myself at Christmas.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.380
I can't afford to make a lot of idle people many.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.390
I hope to support the institutions we've just mentioned.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:51.960
They cost enough.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.550
People are badly off.

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.230
They'd better go there.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.470
Many can't go there.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.470
Many would rather die.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.010
Well, if they'd rather die, they'd better do it.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.160
...and decrease the surplus population.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.200
Besides, excuse me, sir, I don't know that.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.100
But you should know it.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.100
It's not my business, sir.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.430
A man's got enough to do in this world to mind his own business.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.180
Without interfering with a lot of other peoples, mine occupies me constantly.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:16.530
Good evening, sir.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.540
Allow me to express my regret, sir, if I have said anything to you.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:26.920
Good evening.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:30.360
You

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.680
Did I inquire, Mr. Cratchit, what you're doing with that shovelful of coal?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:09.940
I beg your pardon, sir, but the outer office is intensely cold.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.410
And my fire...

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.530
Your fire?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.450
I should have said your fire, sir.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:15.970
Yes, sir.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.280
It shows symptoms of going out.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:22.620
And I thought I might venture to replenish it with a small quantity of coal.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:23.080
Yeah.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.170
Well, of course, you know, it's very evident to me, you know, Mr. Cratchit,

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.250
that you and I left apart.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.310
Oh, I see no ill-pornature.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.480
You don't pay for the coal, so you can afford to be reckless.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.130
Therefore, very evident to me, sir, you know, that my interest is not your interest.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.030
Nor my welfare, your welfare.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.420
Get on with your work, sir. That'll keep you warm enough.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.070
I'm not cold. Why should you be?

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:56.880
And I'm your senior. By a great many years, I fancy.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.540
All about a small shovel full of coal.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.240
None of you are mumbling, you know. None of you are mumbling.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.430
You... you have a wife and family to support, I understand.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.520
Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:19.840
How many children have you got?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.360
Around half a dozen, sir.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.080
Three boys and three girls.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.930
That, that, that. Can I afford a wife?

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:25.690
Yes, sir.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:26.070
Eh?

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.750
I mean, no, sir.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:29.980
Have I...

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.720
I don't know, sir.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.120
Eh?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:34.760
No, no, sir.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.420
How much am I constrained to pay you a week for your services?

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.530
Fifteen shillings.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.970
Be to your interest, sir, to see that you're worth it.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.310
And God save you.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.930
Ah, humbug.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.110
Christmas a humbug?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.290
You can't mean that, I'm sure.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.110
I do mean it, sir.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.880
What right of you to be merry?

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.460
What reason of you to be merry?

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.200
You're poor enough.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:25.900
Come then.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.360
What right of you to be dismal?

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.800
What reason of you to be morose?

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:29.920
You're rich enough.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.900
Oh, don't be cross, Uncle.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.560
How can I help being cross, sir, when I live in such a world of fools as this is?

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.280
Merry Christmas.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.520
What's Christmas time for you, sir?

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:44.450
Time for paying bills without money?

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.950
Time for finding yourself a year older?

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.680
Not a penny of it, sir.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.770
If I had my way, sir, every fool who goes about saying Merry Christmas

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:55.070
will be boiled with his own pudding

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.630
and buried with a stake of olive through his heart.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:58.300
He should.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:58.780
Uncle!

00:09:58.980 --> 00:09:59.340
Nephew!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.260
If you keep Christmas your way, let me keep it in mine.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.840
Keep it? But you don't keep it.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.020
Well, let me leave it around then.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.200
Much good is it done here. Much good will it ever do here.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.410
It's the only time I know of in the long calendar of the year

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:17.910
when men and women seem by one consent to open their shut hearts freely.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:21.730
And therefore, though it's never put a scrap of gold or silver in my pocket,

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.580
I believe it has done me good and will do me good.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.600
And I say, God bless it.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:35.970
Mr. Cratchit, if I hear another word from you, you'll keep your Christmas by losing your situation.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.870
Dear, dear, dear, dear. Quite a powerful speaker, sir.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.590
One of you don't go into Parliament.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.310
Don't be angry, Uncle. Come, dine with us tomorrow.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.370
I'll see you.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:46.770
But why? Why?

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.810
Why did you get married?

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.150
Because I fell in love.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.700
Because I fell in good evening.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.870
You never came to see us before that happened.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.920
Why give that as a reason for not coming now?

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:58.660
Good evening, sir.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:10:59.980
But I want nothing from it.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.200
I ask nothing, aren't you?

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.160
Well, you won't get it, so you won't be disappointed, will you?

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.560
We've never had a quarrel to which I've been partied.

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.200
So why not let us part, Fred?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.560
Good evening, sir.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.730
Well, I'm sorry with all my heart to find you, sir.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.920
But I've made the trial in homage to Christmas.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.660
And I've eaten my Christmas humour to the last.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.540
So a Merry Christmas, Uncle.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:19.380
Good evening, sir.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.640
And a Happy New Year.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.120
You're a noisy devil. That's what you are, sir.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.460
Merry Christmas, Bob Bletchley.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.680
And the same to you, sir, and many of them.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.140
And not forgetting your good lady, Mrs. Fred.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:29.960
Thank you, sir.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.700
A Merry Christmas to you!

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:32.820
A Merry Christmas!

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.130
You're always ready and willing to quit your work, I notice.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.780
It's seven o'clock, sir.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:21.760
That clock's fast.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:27.630
I suppose you'll want all day off tomorrow, eh?

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.370
Well, sir, it is...

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:30.850
It's quite convenient.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:33.720
It isn't convenient. It isn't fair.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:38.380
If I was to stop off account for it, oh, you'd be mightily ill-used.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.300
I'll be bound, wouldn't you?

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.440
Don't think I'm ill-used, do you?

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:46.500
And I have to pay a whole day's wages. No work.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.340
It only happens once a year, sir.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:53.830
That's a pretty excuse for peeking a man's pocket every 25th of December.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.140
Well, I suppose you've got to have it.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:12:59.160
Yeah.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.780
There's the key. You see, sir, that you're here all the earlier, next morning.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.630
Good night, sir, and a merry Christmas.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.290
Bah, humbug.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:00.160
Thank you.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:41.070
Aye, aye, don't stop that noise.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:49.340
My lord, will you make your speech now,

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:53.140
or will you let the ladies and gentlemen continue to enjoy them?

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:57.360
Call silence for the loyal toast.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:15.890
And gentlemen, pray silent for the Right Honourable, the Lord Mayor of London, my lord.

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:28.690
Me lord, ladies and gentlemen, her most gracious majesty, the Queen.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:56.070
I'm glad I'm with you.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:32.850
Thank you.

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:15.040
Well, Ebeneezus, for only you can see me.

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.870
What you want with me?

00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:19.670
Much.

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:22.730
Who are you?

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:26.890
Life, I was your partner, Jacob Marley.

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:28.790
In life!

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:33.950
Why do you trouble me?

00:23:34.190 --> 00:23:40.800
It is required of everyone that the spirit within him should walk abroad among his fellow men.

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:44.960
And if that spirit goes not forth in life, it is...

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:46.960
condemned to do so after death.

00:23:47.140 --> 00:23:54.250
My spirit never walked beyond the narrow limits of our money-changing home.

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:56.520
So I cannot rest.

00:23:57.250 --> 00:23:59.340
I cannot stay.

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:18.270
i cannot linger anywhere you are fitted why i wear the chain i forged in life i made it

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:29.640
link by link you know the weight and length of the coil you bear yourself the words of comfort to me jacob

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.770
speak words of comfort.

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:36.780
I have none to give.

00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:39.180
I am here to warn you,

00:24:39.510 --> 00:24:41.350
to save you, if that be possible.

00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:45.020
To warn? To save me?

00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:47.660
From what?

00:24:48.210 --> 00:24:50.010
From such a fate as mine.

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:51.760
To wander through the world

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:53.800
and witness what I cannot share,

00:24:54.210 --> 00:24:55.710
but might have shared on earth

00:24:55.960 --> 00:24:57.600
and turned to happiness.

00:24:57.960 --> 00:24:59.810
But you...

00:25:00.350 --> 00:25:02.850
We're always a good man of business, Jacob.

00:25:03.190 --> 00:25:03.490
Business.

00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:05.870
Mankind.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:07.400
Be in my business.

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:11.160
Charity, forbearance, benevolence.

00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:12.900
All were my business.

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:15.570
As they should be yours.

00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:21.760
Now heed me, for my time is short.

00:25:22.460 --> 00:25:24.560
You will be haunted by three spirits.

00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:28.270
Without their visits, you cannot hope to shun the path I tread.

00:25:29.540 --> 00:25:29.960
You shall...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:38.290
behold the visions of a christmas past a christmas present and a christmas yet to come

00:25:40.010 --> 00:25:54.030
expect the first when the clock strikes midnight night look to see me no

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:02.680
Thank you.

00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:33.540
Thank you.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:00.790
No!

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:13.560
No!

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:41.520
Christmas pass.

00:27:42.680 --> 00:27:46.480
I am here to show you the things that have been.

00:27:47.620 --> 00:27:51.660
Look back beyond the gulf of vanished years.

00:27:57.060 --> 00:27:58.340
Money in June must be paid.

00:27:58.600 --> 00:27:59.760
But, sir, that's impossible.

00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:03.880
Then I shall have no alternative but to take immediate steps to recover it.

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:07.020
But, sir, you must see that if...

00:28:07.020 --> 00:28:08.500
That is the way I conduct my business.

00:28:11.150 --> 00:28:13.660
You don't mean sell us up.

00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:16.400
That is precisely what I do mean.

00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:20.620
But, sir, I couldn't work in the hospital.

00:28:20.820 --> 00:28:22.560
Mr. Scrooge, I beg on you.

00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:23.080
Good day.

00:28:26.520 --> 00:28:29.020
You can't be so unjust.

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:29.980
Give us a little...

00:28:30.280 --> 00:28:31.570
No time. A week.

00:28:31.730 --> 00:28:32.170
Me.

00:29:08.220 --> 00:29:09.020
Here you come in.

00:29:11.900 --> 00:29:14.240
It is me.

00:29:14.460 --> 00:29:18.510
What they say, that you're a man without pity, without remorse,

00:29:18.980 --> 00:29:21.640
who weighs everything in the scale of profit and loss.

00:29:21.820 --> 00:29:22.060
Bill!

00:29:22.460 --> 00:29:24.880
I couldn't help you.

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:26.460
This is business.

00:29:27.370 --> 00:29:29.630
Why would you allow sentiment to enter this counting house?

00:29:30.090 --> 00:29:31.870
I should be in the bankruptcy court within a year.

00:29:32.580 --> 00:29:34.100
And as for that couple who've just gone out,

00:29:34.360 --> 00:29:36.840
well, you set your mind up the rest about them.

00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:39.260
Worthless, shiftless pair.

00:29:39.960 --> 00:29:41.000
Had my good money.

00:29:41.550 --> 00:29:43.070
Now I want to avoid paying it back.

00:29:43.470 --> 00:29:47.880
Your money. Your money.

00:29:49.930 --> 00:29:51.430
They asked you for a little breathing.

00:29:51.820 --> 00:29:54.240
Just a little time in which to pay. That was all.

00:29:54.400 --> 00:29:55.180
Enough of this, Belle.

00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:57.740
I'm ready to make allowances for your feelings as a woman.

00:29:58.400 --> 00:29:59.980
But I must ask you to leave my business...

00:30:00.710 --> 00:30:04.030
When you marry me, I shall insist.

00:30:09.840 --> 00:30:12.240
I've tried hard not to believe what they've said about you.

00:30:12.640 --> 00:30:14.560
I'd give you anything not to believe it now.

00:30:15.150 --> 00:30:20.660
For the evidence of my own years, I must not always know,

00:30:21.090 --> 00:30:22.610
but I can see now that compassion,

00:30:22.790 --> 00:30:25.130
and one passion only, engrosses you gain.

00:30:26.150 --> 00:30:28.630
But then, even if it were so, I'm not changed towards you.

00:30:28.790 --> 00:30:29.650
You are changed.

00:30:30.640 --> 00:30:37.430
changed in every way. You're not the man. Our contract's an old one, made when we were poor

00:30:37.430 --> 00:30:45.620
and content to be so. May you be happy, alone, the life you've chosen.

00:31:02.080 --> 00:31:07.120
Now look and see the happiness, miss.

00:31:52.030 --> 00:31:58.770
Hi, Belle. I saw an old friend of yours this afternoon.

00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:10.510
you guess how can i i don't know it wasn't mr scrooge mr scrooge it was i passed his office

00:32:10.510 --> 00:32:14.530
window and as it was not shut up and there was a candle inside i could scarcely help see him

00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:24.550
his partners on on the point of death i hear there he sat alone quite alone in the world i do believe

00:32:30.350 --> 00:32:32.090
Spirit, I cannot bear it.

00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:33.780
Haunt me no more.

00:32:34.480 --> 00:32:38.800
I told you these were the shadows of the things that have been.

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:40.740
